/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (The week begins with an overview of Data Engineering as a discipline. Learners explore how modern companies move data across systems and the core components of a data pipeline. Key concepts such as data sources \(APIs, Databases, Logs, IoT\), ETL \(extract, transform, Load\)  vs ELT \(Extract, Load, Transform\), and basic data architecture are introduced.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (A major focus is placed on building data pipelines, which is the backbone of any data engineering workflow. Students learn how data flows through modern systems, how to design structured ETL pipelines, and how to extract data from APIs. Data formats including CSV, JSON, and Parquet are covered, alongside pipeline orchestration and workflow scheduling. Students learn to transform data programmatically and automate data ingestion tasks using scripts.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
