388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (This masterclass goes beyond surface-level AI usage to teach how modern AI systems actually work across the full stack. Participants explore transformer architectures, agentic workflows, GPU computing, and AI inference systems, building an understanding that spans from tokenization and embeddings to CUDA kernels and GPU acceleration. Learners gain the ability to design and optimize production-ready AI solutions. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (Each session combines conceptual learning with practical implementation using the same tools and frameworks used in industry. Participants work with open-source transformer libraries, build agentic workflows with tool calls and APIs, write custom CUDA kernels using Python, and deploy AI workloads across 4 GPUS. Through structured labs and guided experiments, learners gain experience of distributed computing, model sharding, and AI serving. This knowledge is foundational to building real-world AI applications.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (This masterclass emphasizes how AI systems operate in real-world environments where performance, scalability, and reliability matter. Learners examine GPU architectures, model serialization formats, inference engines, and distributed serving strategies used to run modern AI models at scale. By understanding deployment pipelines, performance bottlenecks, and system-level optimization, participants gain the mindset and technical knowledge required to build AI solutions that are not only intelligent but also efficient and deployable in production environments.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
